 "lines": [
  {
   "start": 0.5,
   "end": 4.722,
   "text": "The Pharisees saw his disciples eating with unwashed hands.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 5.022,
   "end": 8.736,
   "text": "Why don't your disciples follow the tradition of the elders?",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 9.136,
   "end": 13.615,
   "text": "You hold on to human rules, and let go of the command of God.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 14.115,
   "end": 19.909,
   "text": "Nothing that goes into a person can make them unclean. It is what comes out of the heart.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 20.609,
   "end": 24.957,
   "text": "Then he went to the region of Tyre. A foreign woman fell at his feet.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 25.257,
   "end": 29.259,
   "text": "Please. My little daughter has an evil spirit.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 29.659,
   "end": 35.842,
   "text": "First let the children eat. It is not right to take the children's bread and throw it to the dogs.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 36.342,
   "end": 42.716,
   "text": "Yes, Lord. But even the dogs under the table eat the children's crumbs.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 43.316,
   "end": 47.577,
   "text": "For such a reply, you may go. The demon has left your daughter.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 48.077,
   "end": 53.014,
   "text": "She went home, and found her child lying on the bed. The demon was gone.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 53.814,
   "end": 58.106,
   "text": "Then some people brought him a man who was deaf, and could hardly speak.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 58.506,
   "end": 64.944,
   "text": "Jesus took him aside, away from the crowd. He put his fingers in his ears, and touched his tongue.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 65.344,
   "end": 68.594,
   "text": "He looked up to heaven, sighed deeply, and said:",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 69.094,
   "end": 70.841,
   "text": "Ephphatha. Be opened.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 71.841,
   "end": 77.668,
   "text": "Immediately his ears were opened, and his tongue was set free. He began to speak plainly.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 78.168,
   "end": 81.892,
   "text": "He has done everything well. He even makes the deaf hear, and the mute speak!",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 82.792,
   "end": 86.108,
   "text": "Follow for part twelve.",
   "tempter": false
  }
 ]
}